---
import Specimen from '../Specimen.astro';
---
<Specimen title="Containers" code={'<div class="container">…</div>          /* 64rem: most content */\n<div class="container-wide">…</div>     /* 80rem: tile grids and product shots */\n<div class="container-narrow">…</div>   /* 43rem: reading width */'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Three widths. Text sits in the narrow or default container; tile grids and product imagery use the wide one.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="containers">
        <div class="box box-wide">container-wide · 80rem</div>
        <div class="box box-default">container · 64rem</div>
        <div class="box box-narrow">container-narrow · 43rem</div>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Grid" code={'<div class="grid grid-2">…</div>  <div class="grid grid-3">…</div>  <div class="grid grid-4">…</div>\n<div class="grid grid-3 shelf-mobile">…</div>  /* a sideways shelf on phones */'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>One column on phones, two on tablets, then two, three or four. On phones, long rows of tiles can become a sideways-scrolling shelf with <code>shelf-mobile</code>.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="grid grid-4">
        {[1, 2, 3, 4].map((n: number) => <div class="cell">{n}</div>)}
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-3 grid-gap">
        {[1, 2, 3].map((n: number) => <div class="cell">{n}</div>)}
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-2 grid-gap">
        {[1, 2].map((n: number) => <div class="cell">{n}</div>)}
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Spacing" surface="none" code={'--space-section  /* between bands: 5rem → 10rem */\n--tile-gap       /* between tiles: 0.75rem → 1.25rem */\n--gutter         /* page edge: 1.25rem → 2.75rem */'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Three fluid spacing tokens do almost all the work. Inside components, spacing follows a 0.25rem step.</p></Fragment>
    <ul class="spacing" role="list">
        <li><span class="bar bar-section"></span><code>--space-section</code><span class="muted">Vertical padding of every band</span></li>
        <li><span class="bar bar-gutter"></span><code>--gutter</code><span class="muted">Distance from the page edge</span></li>
        <li><span class="bar bar-tile"></span><code>--tile-gap</code><span class="muted">Gap between tiles</span></li>
    </ul>
</Specimen>

<style>
    .containers {
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        justify-items: center;
    }

    .box {
        padding: 0.9rem;
        border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
        border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: var(--text-xs);
        text-align: center;
    }

    .box-wide { width: 100%; }
    .box-default { width: 80%; }
    .box-narrow { width: 54%; }

    .cell {
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        height: 5rem;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        background: var(--bg-alt);
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: var(--text-sm);
    }

    .grid-gap {
        margin-top: var(--tile-gap);
    }

    .spacing {
        display: grid;
        gap: 1rem;
    }

    .spacing li {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 12rem) 9rem 1fr;
        gap: 1rem;
        align-items: center;
        font-size: var(--text-sm);
    }

    .bar {
        height: 1rem;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--brand-gradient);
    }

    .bar-section { width: var(--space-section); }
    .bar-gutter { width: var(--gutter); }
    .bar-tile { width: var(--tile-gap); }
</style>
